   above - Traefik's Docker provider reads labels from any container
   with traefik.enable=true, not just ones that also carry a router of
   their own, and crowdsec has no router/web UI to route to.

   The catch (found live): the docker provider still tries to build a
   *service* for every traefik.enable=true container, and with no
   router and no port it fails ("service ... error: port is missing")
   and DISCARDS the whole container's config - including this middleware
   - so every routed service then 404s on "middleware crowdsec@docker
   does not exist". Pointing a (never-routed) service at crowdsec's real
   LAPI port satisfies the provider and lets the middleware register. #}
